              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did kāyccal mean, and what did vali mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: மட்டும்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மட்டும் (maṭṭum) — \"only\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This and nothing beside it. Where English puts only in front of the thing it limits, Tamil hangs மட்டும் (maṭṭum) on the end of it: தண்ணீர் மட்டும் (maṭṭum) — water, and nothing else."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Telugu does the same job with మాత్రమే (mātramē). The doubled ட்ட in the middle is the one held twice, as in ஆகட்டும்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "maṭṭum",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *maṭṭum*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "maṭṭum, then taṇṇīr, and put them in the Tamil order",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *maṭṭum*, then *taṇṇīr*, and put them in the Tamil order]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does மட்டும் (maṭṭum) mean? (\"only\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
