        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: இன்னும்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "இன்னும் (iṉṉum) — \"still, yet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For something that has not finished, and for a bit more of it: இன்னும் (iṉṉum) சிறிது, a little more still. Kannada ಇನ್ನೂ (innū) is the same word; Telugu says ఇంకా (iṅkā)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ன் doubled in the middle is the soft one — the alveolar ன, not the curled ண you have in கிண்ணம். Tamil keeps three of these apart and this word wants the middle one twice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "iṉṉum",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *iṉṉum*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "iṉṉum, then siṟitu, and say the two together",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *iṉṉum*, then *siṟitu*, and say the two together]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does இன்னும் (iṉṉum) mean? (\"still, yet\".) Say it once more."
            }
