          "title": "You'll want to know: சீக்கிரம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சீக்கிரம் (sīkkiram) — \"soon\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Soon, and quickly — Tamil lets one word carry nearness in நேரம் and speed of doing together, and which one is meant comes out of the sentence around it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Set it against பிறகு and the pair covers the whole span: சீக்கிரம் (sīkkiram) is the near end, பிறகு the loose one that promises nothing. Kannada says ಬೇಗ (bēga)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
