          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "முதலில் (mutalil) — \"first of all\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before anything else. It puts an order on things that had none: முதலில் (mutalil) தண்ணீர், பிறகு சாதம் — water to begin with, and the rice after."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With this one you can lay out a sequence end to end: முதலில் (mutalil), then உடனே (uṭaṉē) or சீக்கிரம் (sīkkiram) for what follows fast, then பிறகு for what can wait."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: only, still, soon, at once, and first of all."
            }
          ]
        },
